Hello,
We have an early boot crash in 3.6 and 3.6.1 on many machines, using
nvidia chipsets. Boot fails in 1 case to 10 boots or 9 cases in 10 boots, d=
epending on machine.

The head of log, got via serial console(full log attached):
-------------------------------------------
2.672343=C3=9C BUG: unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at 000=
0000000000010
2.676024=C3=9C IP: =C3=84<ffffffffa001e29c>=C3=9C pacpi_set_dmamode+0x5c/0x=
c0 =C3=84pata_acpi=C3=9C
2.676024=C3=9C PGD 115076067 PUD 1167f1067 PMD 0=20
2.676024=C3=9C Oops: 0000 =C3=84#1=C3=9C PREEMPT SMP=20
2.676024=C3=9C Modules linked in: ata_generic sata_nv pata_acpi libata scsi=
_mod ide_pci_generic ide_core
2.703078=C3=9C CPU 1=20
2.703078=C3=9C Pid: 644, comm: scsi_eh_2 Not tainted 3.6.1-un-def-alt2
#1 System manufacturer System Product Name/M2NPV-VM
-------------------------------------------

Disabling on-board IDE controller in BIOS seems to workarownd the problem.

Regards,
Anton

